{
  "meta": {
    "id": "t1_05",
    "tier": 1,
    "order_in_tier": 5,
    "title": "First Flat & Singing Quarter Melody",
    "composer_source": "Study after Carl Czerny, Op. 599 No. 19",
    "key": {
      "fifths": -1,
      "mode": "major"
    },
    "time_signature": {
      "numerator": 4,
      "denominator": 4
    },
    "target_bpm": 84.0,
    "theory": {
      "summary": "Trains F-major reading (Bb key signature), dotted half notes, and smooth I-IV-ii-V-I triad transitions.",
      "pattern_tip": "Track the shared common tone C4/F3 between F major and Bb/C7 grips so your left hand barely moves.",
      "technique_tip": "Balance the dotted half notes cleanly above quiet blocked triads in the left hand.",
      "ballade_link": "Builds flat-key reading fluency and singing upper-voice phrasing.",
      "concept_title": "Key Signatures (First Flat Bb) & Smooth Common-Tone Voicings",
      "concept_paragraphs": [
        "Welcome to F Major, marked by a single Bb flat in the key signature. Notice how smoothly F (F-A-C), Bb (Bb-D-F), Gm (G-Bb-D), and C7 (C-E-G-Bb) connect using inversions\u2014your Left Hand barely needs to shift position when common tones stay anchored!",
        "Notice the dotted half note filling whole three-beat bars in the melody while gentle triads and V6/5 inversions breathe underneath."
      ],
      "form_map": [
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase A (Bars 1-4)",
          "role": "Singing F-major melody gliding over C7/E (V6/5) to a poised C Half Cadence."
        },
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase B (Bars 5-8)",
          "role": "Expands through warm Bb (IV) and Gm (ii) before resolving authentically to F."
        },
        {
          "phrase_label": "Phrase C (Bars 9-12)",
          "role": "Luminous closing arch reinforcing I - IV - ii - V7 - I."
        }
      ],
      "practice_steps": [
        "1. Locate Bb in both hands so the flat-key grip feels second-nature.",
        "2. Practice Skeleton mode first to see how LH chords pivot around shared notes.",
        "3. Count '1-2-3' steadily through the dotted half notes without cutting beat 3 short.",
        "4. Climb the Tempo Ladder cleanly up to 84 BPM."
      ],
      "audio_examples": [
        {
          "label": "Full F-Major Cadential Circle (I - IV - ii - V7 - I)",
          "caption": "F -> Bb -> Gm -> C7 -> F",
          "chords": [
            "F",
            "Bb",
            "Gm",
            "C7",
            "F"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "Smooth E->F Bass Lift (F -> C7/E -> F)",
          "caption": "1st inversion V6/5 stepping cleanly to Tonic",
          "chords": [
            "F",
            "C7/E",
            "F"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "tempo_marking": "Andante cantabile"
  },
